  "id": "Compound::DB06772 - Gene::10383",
  "verbalization": "Cabazitaxel is linked to Tubb4b through a shared pathway involving Docetaxel, which binds to Tubb4b. This connection is supported by both the direct binding of Docetaxel to Tubb4b and the indirect relationship through Cabazitaxel, which is included in the class of microtubule inhibitors and is associated with Docetaxel. The evidence suggests that Cabazitaxel may act through a mechanism that involves Docetaxel, which in turn interacts with Tubb4b. The lowest common ancestor of Cabazitaxel and Docetaxel points to Tetracyclic Diterpenoid, which may serve as a common intermediary in the biological processes linking these entities. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Tubb4b in the downstream effects of microtubule inhibition, possibly through interactions with Docetaxel.",
